---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="ABQ Waxing — ABQWax.ing"
  description="ABQ waxing is how locals search for Albuquerque waxing. See why the city code plus the service verb makes ABQWax.ing the category-defining domain, offered at $250,000."
  canonical="/abq-waxing/"
  keywords="ABQ waxing, ABQ wax, waxing ABQ, ABQ waxing near me, Albuquerque waxing, ABQWax.ing"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'ABQ Waxing', path: '/abq-waxing/' },
  ]}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-ink-950">
      <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-24">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-400">Albuquerque · ABQ Waxing · The code</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-white sm:text-6xl">
          ABQ waxing — the phrase the domain already says
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-100/85 sm:text-lg">
          ABQ is how Albuquerque is written on tickets, weather maps, and boarding passes. Add waxing and you have the search — and the domain.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-white">
      <div class="container-narrow grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-800 sm:text-base">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">The power of the three-letter city code</h2>
          <p>
            Albuquerque has one shorthand everyone recognizes: <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQ</strong>. It appears on the
            airport code, on local weather apps, and in how people actually type when they search. So when someone looks for
            <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQ waxing</strong>, they are using the city's own vocabulary — and
            <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQWax.ing</strong> is that phrase, complete, in the browser bar.
          </p>
          <p>
            A three-letter code that also works in conversation is scarce. Pairing ABQ with the waxing category leaves a
            competitor with almost no room to own the same phrase, which is exactly what makes the name valuable for a studio,
            a multi-location operator, or a beauty group entering New Mexico.
          </p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">From search to identity</h2>
          <p>
            A domain like this works in every channel at once: it is short enough for a van wrap, precise enough for paid
            search and maps, and memorable enough for word of mouth. Read the
            <a href="/albuquerque-waxing/" class="font-medium text-gold-500 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">full Albuquerque waxing guide</a>
            to see the category it was built to carry.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rounded-3xl border border-ink-100 bg-ink-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-500">The domain</p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">ABQWax.ing</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700">The city code and the service verb, one hostname. No abbreviation needed, no ambiguity left.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-gold-500">$250,000</p>
          <a href="#acquisition" class="btn-primary mt-4">Request terms</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-ink-50">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950 sm:text-4xl">Why ABQ waxing is the search to own</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Exact match</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">The hostname is the query. ABQWax.ing contains ABQ waxing with nothing extra in the way.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Local shorthand</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">ABQ is the market's own abbreviation, so the brand feels native rather than imported.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">The .ing finish</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">The .ing TLD completes the word waxing, turning a label into an action.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
